      "description": "The meme is designed for a broad, general internet audience that may not be specifically aware of or sensitive to ableist stereotypes. The casual, colloquial greeting 'ay man, how ya been?' is commonly used in informal online communication, suggesting the meme targets users who are familiar with this type of internet slang and may not recognize the harmful implications when paired with images of people with Down syndrome.",
